Looking at Cargill role in olive oil vs main transport of bulk oil between
Spain and Italy


*Rubino RS* Tank container intermodali liquidi alimentari | RubinoRS
<https://www.rubinors.com/> is a specialized intermodal logistics company
operating out of Puglia, Italy, that focuses on bulk liquid transport Trasp=
orto
olio Puglia - Tank container alimentari =E2=80=A2 RubinoRS
<https://www.rubinors.com/trasporto-olio/>. While *Cargill* Vegetable oils
| Cargill Food Ingredients EMEA
<https://www.cargill.com/food-beverage/emea/edible-oils/vegetable-oils>
operates extensively in global edible oils and maintains major olive oil
brands in its portfolio Oils | Cargill
<https://www.cargill.com/foodservice/oils>, there is no official, publicly
documented corporate partnership or exclusive logistics contract between
the two entities. [1
<https://www.foodnavigator.com/Article/2007/10/17/cargill-signs-joint-ventu=
re-for-spanish-olive-oil/>
]
The two companies relate only as potential separate entities within the
broader olive oil and liquid food supply chain, operating as follows:

   - *Rubino RS:* Provides specialized Trasporto olio Puglia - Tank
   container alimentari =E2=80=A2 RubinoRS (food-grade tank containers and =
road
   cisterns), handling temperature-controlled and trace-guaranteed logistic=
s
   for the Mediterranean olive oil, wine, and food sectors Azienda di
   trasporti innovativa e efficiente =E2=80=A2 RubinoRS
   <https://www.rubinors.com/azienda-di-trasporti-innovativa-e-efficiente/>=
.
   - *Cargill:* Operates globally in crushing, refining, and bottling oils
   (in countries like Spain and France) and manages retail or foodservice
   olive oil brands Cargill signs joint venture for Spanish olive oil
   <https://www.foodnavigator.com/Article/2007/10/17/cargill-signs-joint-ve=
nture-for-spanish-olive-oil/>
   and Cargill Partners With Filippo Berio Olive Oil
   <https://www.supplysidesj.com/lipids/cargill-partners-with-filippo-berio=
-olive-oil>
   . [1
   <https://www.bakeryandsnacks.com/Article/2004/12/08/Cargill-buys-largest=
-Romanian-sunflower-oil-maker/>,
   2
   <https://www.foodnavigator.com/Article/2007/10/17/cargill-signs-joint-ve=
nture-for-spanish-olive-oil/>
   ]

If you'd like to explore how bulk liquid transport operates, I can help you=
:

   - Review *best practices for olive oil logistics* (temperature, hygiene,
   and tank types).
   - Compare *short-sea shipping versus road freight* for bulk oil
   distribution.
   - Evaluate the *logistical criteria* used to select global food-grade
   transport providers.

Let me know how you would like to *narrow down your research*.

